%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5a0f9465ab7696142ac3a15a37af66c2, type: 3}
  m_Name: Bryan
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  characterId: char_bryan
  displayName: Bryan
  profilePicture: {fileID: 0}
  contactButton: {fileID: 0}
  scheduledMessages:
  - messageId: bryan_introduction
    triggerHour: 20
    triggerMinute: 46
    requiredClues: []
    grantedClues: []
    messages:
    - sender: 1
      text: Hello there, my name is Bryan, a friend of Richard's, Evelyn told me
        to contact you, she is right to be worried, but it's her own fault for opening
        the damned book!
      delay: 0
  - messageId: bryan_richards_strange_actions
    triggerHour: 22
    triggerMinute: 55
    requiredClues: []
    grantedClues:
    - what_is_richard_doing
    messages:
    - sender: 1
      text: Richard is acting strange, he is wandering around the house, staring
        and clocks, checking cabinets, locking and unlocking display cases... Thought
        you ought to know.
      delay: 0
  questions:
  - questionId: Q01B
    questionText: What do you know about 'Count Backward'?
    askOnce: 1
    requiredClues:
    - backstory
    grantedClues:
    - bryans_knowledge
    response:
    - sender: 1
      text: Count Backward is, according to legend, a spirit which arrives at gatherings
        on New Years Eve, but only if invited.
      delay: 5.3
    - sender: 1
      text: Count Backward is then 'given license' (As the legend says) to inhabit
        the mind and body of one of the attendees for the duration. If he is not
        told to leave by midnight, he will reset time for the guests in a never ending
        cycle in which, they never see the new year.
      delay: 2.3
  - questionId: Q02B/A
    questionText: How do you know so much about the Count?
    askOnce: 1
    requiredClues:
    - bryans_knowledge
    - backstory
    grantedClues:
    - 
    response:
    - sender: 1
      text: I am a historian, you see, and I dabble in legend from time to time,
        though granted, this is somewhat of a niche one.
      delay: 3.1
  - questionId: Q02B/B
    questionText: What do you know of a diary?
    askOnce: 1
    requiredClues:
    - backstory
    - the_diary
    - bryans_knowledge
    grantedClues:
    - evelyn_bryan_confrontation
    response:
    - sender: 1
      text: Honestly? I hid it, you see myself and Evelyn historically aren't on
        the best of terms, and I used to play sort of pranks on her to give her a
        fright. I placed the diary without her knowledge many years ago
      delay: 2.8
    - sender: 1
      text: I had completely forgotten about the diary, until Evelyn confronted me
        about it earlier, at around 8:30
      delay: 1.8
  - questionId: Q03B
    questionText: What came of your confrontation with evelyn?
    askOnce: 1
    requiredClues:
    - evelyn_bryan_confrontation
    - backstory
    - the_diary
    - bryans_knowledge
    grantedClues:
    - 
    response:
    - sender: 1
      text: I told her to give it back, and forget that she had read any of it.
      delay: 2.8
    - sender: 1
      text: You see, a few years after hiding it I was researching an unrelated matter,
        when I stumbled across an old newspaper article which to my surprise mentioned
        the Count, and when I looked it, I found tens, ney, hundreds of testimonies,
        always on the eve of a new year, writing his name apparently had no effect
        any other day of the year.
      delay: 1.8
    - sender: 1
      text: The testimonies almost always mentioned of a guest acting strange after
        his name had been written down- remembering events that only occured later
        in the evening, and having impossible knowledge.
      delay: 2.2
    - sender: 1
      text: I'm not usually a believer in the supernatural but this... it gave me
        chils.
      delay: 3
  - questionId: Q04B/A
    questionText: How long have you known Richard?
    askOnce: 1
    requiredClues:
    - backstory
    - the_diary
    - richard_bryan_relationship
    grantedClues:
    - 
    response:
    - sender: 1
      text: My entire life! We attended primary school togethor, and have been friends
        ever since.
      delay: 2.8
  - questionId: Q04B/B
    questionText: Richard said you know a lot about the textiles industry?
    askOnce: 1
    requiredClues:
    - richard_bryan_relationship
    - bryans_textile_knowledge
    grantedClues:
    - richards_faulty_memory_2
    response:
    - sender: 1
      text: Yes! Well... I'm no expert of course, but it's interesting! I briefly
        worked with Richard in their family mill in my early 20s.
      delay: 3
  - questionId: Q06B
    questionText: Richard said that you knew each other from secondary school, not
      primary school.
    askOnce: 1
    requiredClues:
    - richard_bryan_relationship
    - bryans_textile_knowledge
    - bryans_faulty_memory
    grantedClues: []
    response:
    - sender: 1
      text: Secondary school? Yes. Sorry. I pictured us much younger.
      delay: 4.3
  - questionId: Q08B/A
    questionText: Richard's pocket watch is missing, did you see anybody leave the
      drawing room in the last twenty or so minutes?
    askOnce: 1
    requiredClues:
    - missing_pocket_watch
    grantedClues:
    - stolen_pocket_watch?
    response:
    - sender: 1
      text: Oh no! Thats terrible. Its okay, Richard will forgive the person who
        stole it.
      delay: 2.1
    - sender: 1
      text: I've been speaking to Grace for the past twenty minutes, so no, I didn't
        see anything.
      delay: 3.8
  - questionId: Q08B/B
    questionText: What do you mean? 'the person who stole it'? Nobody is implying
      it is stolen.
    askOnce: 1
    requiredClues:
    - stolen_pocket_watch?
    grantedClues: []
    response:
    - sender: 1
      text: Ah quite, yes... It may not have been stolen, but we're at a party, its
        seems likely? no?
      delay: 6.2
  - questionId: Q10B
    questionText: What did you mutter to yourself immediately after the loud crash?
    askOnce: 1
    requiredClues:
    - what_did_bryan_say
    grantedClues: []
    response:
    - sender: 1
      text: I don't recall muttering anything to myself. Perhaps it was my gasp at
        the surprise crashing sound?
      delay: 1.2
  - questionId: Q12B
    questionText: Why did you say 'I'm glad that he has forgiven you' to Alex, you
      were unaware of what he had done, were you not?
    askOnce: 1
    requiredClues:
    - what_bryan_whispered_to_alex
    grantedClues:
    - bryan_says_alex_lies
    response:
    - sender: 1
      text: I don't know what your talking about. Alex is lying. Richard already
        forgave him more than half an hour ago.
      delay: 2
